# Context

## Background
Workstream 2 of plans/2026-11-09-upstream-alignment.md: discussion and
upload UX ported from upstream lawn.

## Why This Way
- CSV export is dashboard-only and audience-aware: buildCommentsCsv
  filters rows by audience ("all" = team+share for the dashboard;
  "share" exists for a possible future share-viewer export). Reviewers
  traced every export and render path: team-audience text cannot reach
  a share viewer.
- commentLinks.ts is the final upstream parser (after the 4e87d99
  linear-time fix); candidates are re-validated with new URL so
  javascript:/data:/vbscript: never linkify even if the regex drifts.
- CollapsibleSidebar uses useSyncExternalStore with a server snapshot
  that never reads storage (the 251e899 hydration pattern) and is
  inert (inert + aria-hidden + pointer-events-none + blur) when
  collapsed. The share page was deliberately not wired: its comments
  are a stacked section, not a side panel.
- Upload errors keep our coded ConvexError {code, message} contract;
  uploadErrors.ts maps message -> per-code fallback -> generic. The
  backend messages are already user-facing.
- The built-in sidebar toggle is suppressed (toggle={() => null});
  the discussion header button drives the persisted store directly.

## Gotchas
- ALLOWED_UPLOAD_CONTENT_TYPES is now exported for its test; keep it
  in sync with DropZone copy and the -layout.tsx drag regex (no AVI:
  backend rejects it).
- Videos table audience field flows into CSV rows via
  api.comments.getThreaded; if that query ever strips fields, the
  export silently degrades - the call site was checked, not the query.

